    "body": "## Summary\n\n**ADR-053 — honor viewport units in max-width/max-height clamps.** One commit. **Docs follow after merge.**\n\nCloses another sticky-sidebar prerequisite: `max-width: 100vw`, `max-height: 100vh`, and `max-height: calc(100vh - 48px)` now clamp for the first time.\n\n## What changed\n\n### `src/renderer/layout/layout.cpp` — 4 lines removed\n\n```diff\n-        if (auto xw = style->get(\"max-width\")) {\n-            if (!is_auto(*xw) && *xw != \"none\" &&\n-                xw->find(\"vw\") == std::string::npos &&\n-                xw->find(\"vh\") == std::string::npos) {\n+        if (auto xw = style->get(\"max-width\")) {\n+            if (!is_auto(*xw) && *xw != \"none\") {\n```\n\nSame for `max-height` (minus the `%` guard, which stays — that's `parent_content_height` threading territory).\n\n**Preserved:**\n- `%` guard on `max-height` (separate concern)\n- `> 0.0f` safety checks (initial render safety net — ADR-037 needed this but didn't trust it; it was already in the code)\n\n### `tests/test_box_model.cpp` — 1 flipped, 3 added\n\n**Flipped in place:**\n```\nold: \"max-width: containing vw is skipped (not collapsed)\"\n     CHECK(width == 400)  // guard skipped the clamp\nnew: \"max-width: containing vw now clamps (ADR-053)\"\n     CHECK(width == 100)  // min(100px, 75vw) @ vw=800 -> 100\n```\nThis test was **explicitly written to guard the old skip behavior**. After ADR-053 it asserts the correct clamped value. Tagged `[adr-039][adr-053]`.\n\n**3 new tests** (each forces the clamp to actually fire by setting explicit 5000px natural size — otherwise the natural size is already below the max and the clamp no-ops):\n\n| Test | CSS | Viewport | Expect |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `100vw` clamp | `width:5000px; max-width:100vw` | 800×600 | `width == 800` |\n| `100vh` clamp | `height:5000px; max-height:100vh` | 800×600 | `height == 600` |\n| `calc(100vh - 48px)` clamp | `height:5000px; max-height:calc(100vh - 48px)` | 800×600 | `height == 552` |\n\n**Test helper extended**: `run()` gains `float viewport_height = 0.0f`, forwards to the 6-arg `layout()` overload. Default protects all existing callers — zero test churn.\n\n## Verification\n\n```\nAll tests passed (2471 assertions in 647 test cases)\n```\n\n- 644 → 647 cases (+3 new tests)\n- 2465 → 2471 assertions (+6 new)\n- Zero pre-existing tests broken except the one deliberately flipped\n\n## Honest delta framing\n\n**Zero visible PNG delta.** `.vector-sticky-pinned-container` is `h=0` from ancestor culling; the clamp fires but the element has nothing to clamp. Same category as ADR-047/048: correct infrastructure before consumer.\n\n**What changes semantically**: three viewport-unit max clamps now compute correct pixel values. Any future un-culling immediately gets a correctly-clamped box.\n\n## Honest correction\n\nADR-053 spec claimed \"no existing test relies on unclamped behavior.\" **That claim was wrong.** One test did — `\"max-width: containing vw is skipped (not collapsed)\"` — and it was the exact test that needed to flip. Updated in place with an explanatory comment, per the pattern ADR-051 used when `parse_operand` discovery forced a test change.\n\n## Prerequisite chain\n\n| Layer | Status |\n|---|---|\n| `@supports (display: grid)` gate | ✅ ADR-050 |\n| `calc(100vh - 48px)` parses | ✅ ADR-051 |\n| `viewport_h` in production | ✅ ADR-052 |\n| Layout reads `max-height` | ✅ **ADR-053 (this PR)** |\n| Ancestor culling | ❌ pending (separate) |\n| `position: sticky` scroll-Y | ❌ pending (separate) |\n\n## Test count\n\n- 647 cases / 2471 assertions all pass\n- +3 new tests / +6 new assertions\n- 1 test flipped in place (guard → clamp)\n\nRefs #240\n",
